          "text": "Skin lesions"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports about 1–2 weeks of lesions, initially a small red spot on the right shin that blistered and developed yellow/honey-coloured crust; thinks they are spreading. Examination: 3 superficial lesions on the right anterior shin, 0.5–1.5 cm, with erythematous bases and honey-coloured crust; 1 similar lesion, about 1 cm, on the left dorsal forearm. Mildly excoriated and non-tender. No surrounding cellulitis or abscess; no bullae; no face or oral lesions."
      }
